    "body": "Great on any Friday: Google Pixel Buds Pro 2 (2025) - Bluetooth Earbuds with Active Noise Cancellation\nNobody Wants This Brabus Mercedes-AMG G 63, Super SUV Fails To Sell\n16 photos\nPhoto: Cars&Bids\nWell, it’s not like it hasn’t sparked any interest, because it has, though it hasn’t gotten that much so that it could actually find a new home for itself. Therefore, this Brabus-tuned Mercedes-AMG G 63 is still for sale in the United States of America.\nIt is a 2021 model year that has seen plenty of action, as it had 66,500 miles (107,000 km) on the odo at the time of cataloging. There are some creases and wear and the driver’s seat, and there is curb rash on the right rear wheel. Other than that, there is nothing wrong with this modified super SUV.\nThings such as the front and rear bumpers, fender flares, hood, roof spoiler, and spare wheel cover have come from the aftermarket world, and they are part of the Brabus Widestar package. This Mercedes-AMG G 63 also features new 23-inch Brixton Forged wheels, a starry sky headliner, a Stage 1 ECU tune, and a Capristo exhaust system.\nAs a result, it should pump out more oomph, though since a dyno chart hasn’t been provided, we do not know the revised output and thrust. The standard model has 577 hp (585 ps/430 kW) and 627 lb-ft (850 Nm) of torque on tap from its bi-turbo 4.0-liter V8 engine. It needs 4.3 seconds to hit 60 mph (97 kph) from zero for the latest model year (2027), which has an MSRP of $198,750 in our market.\nPhoto: Cars&Bids A 360-degree camera system, triple-locking differentials, heated and ventilated front seats with power adjustment, heated rear seats, a heated steering wheel, Nappa leather upholstery, and a Burmester sound system are some of the features mentioned in the ad when it comes to the pictured Mercedes-AMG G 63.\nThe premium truck with Brabus mods has had its engine, brakes, and battery system checked in May 2026, at 59,040 miles (95,016 km), the eporative vent purge valve, charcoal/vapor canister, and wheels replaced the month before, at 58,519 miles (94,177 km), and that is also when the engine oil and filter were changed. Other service entries as being revealed in the ad, including in January 2026, December 2025, August 2025, May 2024, and so on.\nIt’s been reported that the seller purchased this Mercedes-AMG G 63 new back in November 2021. The vehicle, which is accompanied by the Brabus build invoices, two keys, and a build sheet, is titled to their LLC, and as we already told you, it is still for sale.\nThis ride was advertised on Cars&Bids, where the gavel hit the table on November 25, 2026, and since the reserve was not met, the truck failed to sell. The highest bid was $120,500, and if you feel that this tuned G-Wagen is worth more, then feel free to contact the seller here .\nLiked the article? Follow us to see more stories from autoevolution in your Google feeds.\nmercedes-amg g 63 Mercedes g 63 amg G 63 Brabus for sale used cars auction\nAbout the author: Cristian Gnaticov\nAfter a series of unfortunate events put an end to Cristian's dream of entering a custom built & tuned old-school Dacia into a rally competition, he moved on to drive press cars and write for a living. He's worked for several automotive online journals and now he's back at autoevolution after his first tour in the mid-2000s. Full profile\nUP NEXT Teen Got New 1966 Shelby GT350, Policeman Bought It To Keep Him out of Jail, Family had It 50 Years",
